  "verdict": "GO -- the ADJECTIVE boundary EMERGE-72 named is SURPASSED by the adjective's OWN ATTRIBUTIVE PRE-NOMINAL POSITION cue. The corpus's adjectives (big/small/fast/tall/grey/...) are high-FREQUENCY AND high-context-COVERAGE, so EMERGE-62's 2-cue Goldilocks discovery MISLABELS 2-4 of them CLOSED per seed; the position statistic attribscore[w] = fraction of w's occurrences where w is PRECEDED by a closed word AND FOLLOWED by a content noun (the DET _ NOUN attributive slot -- Tomasello/Goldberg attributive construction, the pre-nominal modifier slot; the INVERSE-position cue to EMERGE-62b's function-word cue; Yang-Getz 2026 3rd property; catalog G.12) RECLASSIFIES them OPEN (attributive-rate >= 0.5: adjectives sit at 0.68-0.74, the true closed class at <= 0.36). Adjective reclassification F1 1.000 (all mislabelled adjectives promoted OPEN, ZERO true function words promoted). With the adjectives OPEN, the producer ADMITS + MINES + RENDERS the corpus-attested adjective constructions -- attributive 'the big owl can fly' (det ADJ subj can verb) + predicative 'the owl is big' (det subj is ADJ) -- for a total of 7 DISTINCT constructions (>= 7), all rendered EXACT on spikes (render 1.000; the 5-slot C_ATTRIB fits N_SLOT_POOLS=6). Every input-destruction/hold-out control COLLAPSES: POSITION-SHUFFLE (scramble word positions before the attributive stat) -> 0 adjectives reclassified -> 0 adjective constructions mined (the cue is LOAD-BEARING, not spurious); FREQUENCY-ONLY (the EMERGE-62 2-cue baseline, no position cue) -> 0 adjective constructions -> the EMERGE-72 5-construction state (proving the position cue is what ADDS the adjectives, 5.0 rendered); NO-CORPUS -> 0 registered; HELD-OUT-CONSTRUCTION -> the shared det+subj+verb backbone recovered from the OTHERS (1.000). The gate-first no-confab MOAT holds BY CONSTRUCTION: 0 producer invocations on abstains. 6 seeds. ==> the producer renders a BROADER, corpus-driven, router-selected inventory including the adjective constructions -- the broadening is CORPUS-POSITION-DRIVEN (position-shuffle collapses it). HONEST SCOPE: BROADENS the bounded, corpus-attested, router-selected inventory from 5 to >= 7 (adds the adjective's attributive-position cue), NOT open prose (R4). The A->W spell stays the token surface; the fully-spiking A->W of the NEW adjective content words is the EMERGE-67/68-style follow-on. Reuse-by-import; NO sim/ edit; moat untouched.",
  "go": true,
  "mechanism": "CLOSE the adjective boundary EMERGE-72 named by adding the ADJECTIVE's OWN ATTRIBUTIVE PRE-NOMINAL POSITION as a distributional cue. The 2-cue Goldilocks discovery (frequency + coverage) mislabels the corpus's high-frequency, high-coverage adjectives CLOSED; the position statistic attribscore = fraction of occurrences in the DET _ NOUN attributive slot (preceded by a closed word, followed by a content noun) reclassifies them OPEN (ASYMMETRIC: only promotes a Goldilocks-CLOSED word; never demotes an open word or a true determiner). With the adjectives OPEN, the extended labeller admits a pre-nominal ADJ slot (attributive) + a predicative post-copular ADJ slot, so the EMERGE-72 signature-keyed registry mines + renders the attributive + predicative adjective constructions -> >= 7 constructions on spikes. INVERSE-position cue to EMERGE-62b's function-word cue; Tomasello usage-based / Goldberg attributive construction (the pre-nominal modifier slot); Yang-Getz 2026 3rd property; Redington/Cartwright-Brent neighbour role; catalog G.12 Broca open/closed. POSITION-SHUFFLE / FREQUENCY-ONLY / NO-CORPUS / HELD-OUT-CONSTRUCTION input-destruction controls gate the result. Reuse-by-import; NO sim/ edit; gate-first moat untouched.",
